<title>ITALY: Second United DC-10-30F conversion delivery.</title>
<headline>Second United DC-10-30F conversion delivery.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The second reconfigured Douglas McDonnell DC-10-30F cargo aircraft for use by United Airlines Inc on domestic and Asian routes will handed over by the Officine Aeronavali di Venezia late this week or early next week, industry sources said.</p>
<p>Conversion work has been carried out by the Venice unit, itself part of the Alenia group. The first converted DC-10-30F was handed over on February 26.</p>
<p>Two further DC-10-30s will arrive in Italy for conversion during April and May with the work completed by late August to mid-September.</p>
<p>The converted aircraft can each carry up to 68 tonnes.</p>
<p>--Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44-171-542-7706 Fax 5017</p>
